00:49:13,153 --> 00:49:13,373
Yup.

468
00:49:13,553 --> 00:49:15,094
Episode 43, we talked about that.

469
00:49:15,314 --> 00:49:16,455
India, episode 119.

470
00:49:16,922 --> 00:49:22,685
Meanwhile, the East African Rift Zone is an area where that continental landmass is splitting.

471
00:49:23,385 --> 00:49:26,547
But this is constantly happening through time.

472
00:49:26,947 --> 00:49:30,728
So there's been discussion that I've read about what counts as a supercontinent.

473
00:49:31,089 --> 00:49:35,671
There have, you will be unsurprised to hear, been other terms proposed.

474
00:49:36,464 --> 00:49:47,428
So, you will see sometimes, and we will mention later in this episode, the term "megacontinent" for a continent that's impressive but not quite a supercontinent.

