00:49:55,190 --> 00:50:00,212
But cratons are sort of the ancient cores of our modern continents.

477
00:50:00,625 --> 00:50:13,690
The parts of the continent that have been around since, for billions of years, that themselves may have come together in the past to landmasses that may or may not count as a supercontinent, depending on who you're asking.

478
00:50:14,490 --> 00:50:23,913
So there has been a lot of continental conglomeration and assemblage over the eons, some of which may or may not actually count as supercontinent.

479
00:50:24,469 --> 00:50:33,692
So in our discussion today, there will be a number of times where I say the name of an ancient supercontinent, and then add the caveat that not everybody agrees that this counts as a supercontinent.

