01:54:55,382 --> 01:55:03,646
We are still in the supercontinent cycle. In fact, there is both breakup and assembly happening today.

918
01:55:04,446 --> 01:55:07,007
Pangaea continues to break apart today.

919
01:55:07,387 --> 01:55:15,471
The African Rift Zone, the East African Rift, is a place where the crust along East Africa is splitting apart.

920
01:55:15,891 --> 01:55:19,773
That is the continued breakup of the Pangaean land masses.

921
01:55:20,366 --> 01:55:25,087
At the same time, new continental pieces continue to come together.

922
01:55:25,868 --> 01:55:34,611
A lot of those pieces that were separate, North China, South China, during Pangaea, are now part of what we call Eurasia, which is Europe and Asia.

923
01:55:35,171 --> 01:55:43,714
India moved up from Gondwana into Asia within the last 50 million years, joined about 50 million years ago.

924
01:55:44,226 --> 01:55:49,528
Australia is moving north. It is on its way up towards Eurasia.

925
01:55:50,028 --> 01:55:58,951
So we are in a period of overlap between continued breakup and the assembly of what will eventually be a new supercontinent.

926
01:55:59,431 --> 01:56:04,753
In fact, Eurasia has been considered by some to be a megacontinent.

927
01:56:04,793 --> 01:56:07,693
Yeah, that could be our next Gondwana.

928
01:56:07,905 --> 01:56:16,649
Yes, because it includes the North China craton, the South China craton, Siberia, now India, Australia's on its way.

929
01:56:17,089 --> 01:56:27,934
That might be our next megacontinent that heralds, like the Silver Surfer, the arrival of a future supercontinent.

