1077
02:07:17,928 --> 02:07:24,111
and more towards what pieces should be present in this ecosystem that make it healthy.

1078
02:07:24,531 --> 02:07:30,573
To the effect that I doubt we're going to focus on removing a lot of invasive species.

1079
02:07:31,233 --> 02:07:34,875
Like the pythons. I don't know that we need to remove all the pythons.

1080
02:07:35,386 --> 02:07:38,387
If the ecosystem can build around that.

1081
02:07:38,907 --> 02:07:45,130
And I'm sure that you will still find debate between how we need to prioritize.

1082
02:07:45,150 --> 02:07:50,092
Because what you're dealing with now is two different philosophies.

1083
02:07:50,652 --> 02:07:57,335
Is the priority the fact that the yellow-bellied warbler or whatever is about to disappear?

1084
02:07:58,026 --> 02:08:02,767
Is about to be lost from our natural wild record for forever?

1085
02:08:03,268 --> 02:08:07,009
Or is it more important that the Everglades continues to be a habitat?

1086
02:08:08,189 --> 02:08:12,571
And depending on who you ask, they may staunchly be like,

1087
02:08:13,031 --> 02:08:18,733
yes, the Everglades is important, but absolutely so is this individual species.

1088
02:08:18,833 --> 02:08:22,355
And you may have other people go, if we can save the species, great.

1089
02:08:23,445 --> 02:08:27,447
Celebration all around, but I really only care that the Everglades stays healthy.

1090
02:08:27,807 --> 02:08:34,550
And there's not necessarily that one is wrong, it's just they're coming at it from different priorities and different mentalities.

1091
02:08:35,030 --> 02:08:38,011
And with that in mind, to answer Mike's question,

1092
02:08:38,531 --> 02:08:46,615
arguably the point at which there is kind of a no return that any more interference is just interference.

1093
02:08:47,186 --> 02:08:51,327
Arguably that happens the minute an invasive species is introduced.

1094
02:08:51,947 --> 02:08:58,110
Unless you can just really put forth a major hunting effort, which has happened.

1095
02:08:58,130 --> 02:09:02,792
There have been moments where we have gone through and basically, at least from regions,

1096
02:09:03,352 --> 02:09:05,633
eliminated certain invasive things.

1097
02:09:05,773 --> 02:09:09,914
Or reintroduced something that was extirpated from a region and put it back.

1098
02:09:10,784 --> 02:09:17,347
But it doesn't take very long for that space in the ecosystem, for the ecosystem to conform.

1099
02:09:17,367 --> 02:09:22,489
To be to that gap or to that new thing, like a tree growing around a fence.

1100
02:09:23,149 --> 02:09:25,870
Ecosystems develop their own equilibrium.

1101
02:09:26,411 --> 02:09:30,372
And this is one of the biggest cautions in conservation.

1102
02:09:30,512 --> 02:09:35,034
And we've learned this lesson in the past, we don't want to just start poking at them.

1103
02:09:35,205 --> 02:09:38,607
Because even if it feels like we're going to make the right choice,

1104
02:09:39,307 --> 02:09:46,510
they are such intricate systems that it pays to have a really thorough understanding of ecosystem dynamics.

1105
02:09:47,051 --> 02:09:51,193
Before we start trying to remove or introduce new things.

1106
02:09:51,433 --> 02:09:56,455
Well there also is kind of the bigger picture aspect of just time marching on.

1107
02:09:56,495 --> 02:10:00,337
That you will never make that ecosystem what it was yesterday.

1108
02:10:00,524 --> 02:10:01,704
No, you can't go back.

1109
02:10:01,864 --> 02:10:05,426
It will never be what it was in the 50s because it's not the 50s anymore.

1110
02:10:06,086 --> 02:10:11,328
Things have changed, the climate has shifted, the continents are shifting.

1111
02:10:12,488 --> 02:10:20,651
You will never ever have Africa or North America or South America or Australia as it once was.

1112
02:10:21,211 --> 02:10:22,172
It's just not going to happen.

1113
02:10:22,352 --> 02:10:23,372
Only as it will be.

1114
02:10:23,703 --> 02:10:37,630
So there's a big mentality in a lot of conservation circles that is also this idea of going back to how it should be is a faulty concept in and of itself.

1115
02:10:37,790 --> 02:10:44,313
Because there is no should. Things have and always will be constantly changing.

1116
02:10:44,873 --> 02:10:46,614
So there is no ideal state.

1117
02:10:46,865 --> 02:10:51,327
Long term health and stability of the ecosystem might be more important.

1118
02:10:52,127 --> 02:10:56,489
